    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0584" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6329</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt
                        to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-11">March 11, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I think this telegram<anchor n="45" xml:id="d734-f1"/> in regard to the China
                    Consortium goes much too far. I have, therefore, struck out the paragraphs that
                    seem to me unnecessary. I do not think it is necessary for us to give approval
                    at this late date to the old Consortium agreement, especially in the way it has
                    worked out.</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d734-f1" n="45" xml:id="d734-f1-content">
                <p>See letter from the Secretary of State to President Roosevelt, March 2, <ref
                        target="#pg571">p. 571</ref>; for telegram as sent to the Ambassador in the
                    United Kingdom, see <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
